From 7580ff7e71a3eafcf160ad2d4d8aa6683f14fdd0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jaishil-Patel <jaishilpatel1105@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 11 Sep 2026 09:42:58 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] Port to ROS 2 Humble / Ignition Fortress, and add the
 missing sensors

Upstream (Sekkat et al.) targets Galactic in Docker. This is the port to Humble on
WSL2, plus the three sensors the model was missing entirely.

pepper_robot.gazebo shipped 28 sensor *frames* -- empty links behind fixed joints --
and zero <sensor> elements, so nothing published depth, scan or IMU. Proposal S4.4.2
fixes the observation modality as depth-based and identical across both branches, so
this blocked the RL task outright. Added camera_depth (320x240, 58 deg, 0.4-8 m, 15 Hz)
on Head, front_laser (gpu_lidar, 15 samples, 60 deg, 0.1-3 m, 10 Hz) on Tibia, and
imu_torso (100 Hz) on base_link.

Sensors attach to real parent links with explicit poses reproducing the frame offsets,
not to the sensor frames themselves: URDF->SDF collapses those massless links into SDF
<frame> elements, so <gazebo reference="CameraDepth_frame"> would not resolve.
