enable_moveit:=false, added in the previous commit, wedged the simulator on its own.
robot_state_publisher lives inside move_group.launch.py, and gz_ros2_control blocks in
its Configure waiting for that node's /robot_state_publisher/get_parameters service.
Blocking there blocks the whole simulation loop, so the world advertised
/world/<w>/stats and then never stepped: `ign topic -e` on it hung forever, the robot
never finished spawning, and the only symptom was "robot_state_publisher service not
available, waiting again..." repeating at 2 Hz.

The xacro arguments are deliberately the same ones move_group.launch.py passes, so the
robot description is identical whichever path launches it. A description that differed
between them would put a difference into the experiment that has nothing to do with
geometry, which is the one thing S4.4.2 requires the branches to differ by.
