Subject: [PATCH 4/7] Add a base contact sensor and its ROS 2 bridge, for real
 collision detection

C_i in Eq. 4.1 and CR in Eq. 4.5 need a collision signal, and until now nothing
provided one: collision.source defaulted to 'contact' in rl/config/env.yaml with no
contact sensor anywhere in the model, so the env refused to start. Adds
ign_base_contact (type="contact", on Tibia_collision -- the mobile base's own
collision element in the generated model.sdf), gated by its own sensor_contact switch
so `sensors:=false` still turns everything off, mirroring the depth/lidar/imu pattern.

Bridged as `contacts` in bridge.launch.py (ignition.msgs.Contacts ->
ros_ign_interfaces/msg/Contacts, IGN default /bumper, ROS default
/pepper_robot/bumper), matching rl.sim_process.BUMPER_TOPIC and
RosInterface.CONTACT_TOPIC exactly -- the same identifier is now the single source of
truth across the launch files and the env.

Also caught two things while wiring this up, both from getting collision detection
verified rather than assumed:
  - XML comments may not contain a double hyphen; the prose style throughout this
    project's docs is full of them, and this is the second time it has bitten an edit
    to this file.
  - ros_ign_bridge's Contacts conversion was already present in the vendored ros_ign
    checkout (ros_ign_interfaces/msg/Contact{,s}.msg, convert/ros_ign_interfaces.cpp),
    so no change was needed there -- confirmed by inspection before wiring the bridge
    entry, not assumed.
