From b1a15b00437d2348d81c8f7a376f8eb833a71d58 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jaishil-Patel <jaishilpatel1105@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 18:32:28 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] Make the simulated base drivable and the whole body
 collision-sensed

The base could not drive, the joints were limp and the posture was wrong, so the
simulated Pepper did not match the real one. Measured and fixed 28 Sep - 1 Oct 2026.

Drivetrain (pepper_drive_wheels.xacro, ign_virtual_diff_drive):
- DiffDrive on two of the three 120-degree omni wheels made them fight; a forward
  command drove her 0.2 m backwards and tipped her. Two virtual coaxial drive wheels
  (r 0.072, 0.31 m apart) now sit at the base centre and carry the traction; the real
  wheels are frictionless supports, so the support polygon is the real robot's.
  Tracking 84-99% (straight, slow, reverse, spins, arcs), tilt <= 3.5 deg.
- Rejected and recorded in the xacro: VelocityControl (tips over), larger wheels,
  centreline casters (tips in arcs), a sprung axle (DART lets the light wheel link sink
  and lose grip), and a tripod (CoM only 9 mm behind the axle).

Controllers and posture:
- With enable_moveit:=false no ros2_control controller was ever spawned, so every
  joint was limp. gz.launch.py now spawns the controllers listed in
  moveit_controller_manager.yaml plus joint_state_broadcaster.
- ign_ros2_control ignores <param name="initial_position">; added initial_value on
  the position state interface of 45 joints, so head and arms start in the real pose.

Collision sensing:
- Contact sensors on 16 links: base shell, torso, hip, pelvis, neck, head, shoulders,
  biceps, elbows, forearms and hands. The base alone missed side-on bumps, and the
  hip/pelvis gap let Pepper wedge under a legless scanned chair seat uncounted.
---
